; =============================================================================
;  ATS 2.50  -  BBC Advanced Teletext System ROM, for the BBC Micro / Master
;  Commented disassembly of ATS250.ROM (16K, &8000-&BFFF)
; =============================================================================
;
;  Generated by dis.py from ats250.json + ats250.ann. Labels and comments are
;  an analyst's reconstruction, not the BBC's source. See the Advanced Teletext
;  System User Guide (1986) for the documented interface.
;
;  WHAT THE ROM DOES
;  A complete rewrite of Acorn's TFS 1.03 for the same Teletext Adapter:
;    - a "page grabber" in the interrupt handler with 20 records, each naming a
;      page (magazine, page, sub-code) and a buffer to store it in
;    - OSWORD &7A calls 0-27 (numbered, not &80+ as in TFS)
;    - * commands: TELETEXT TTXON/OFF HON HOFF MAGAZINE BBC CH ITV S4C NOTTX
;      TUNE TIME DATE PAGE TRANSFER DATA DISPLAY TELESOFT (any command may
;      take extra leading T's: *TTIME)
;    - a terminal with Fastext-style coloured links, kept pages, previous page,
;      sub-page entry, status page, live subtitles and CRC colouring
;    - a Telesoftware terminal that reads the broadcast catalogue and downloads
;      files to disc, network or tape, block by block
;    - support for the Master 128 (hidden-RAM workspace, service calls &22-&27)
;  It is not a filing system: Telesoftware is downloaded with OSWORD 24.
;
;  ADAPTER REGISTERS (as for TFS 1.03)
;    &FC10 r: b7 INT, b6 DOR, b4 FSYN, b3-b0 links    w: b0-1 channel,
;          b2 capture, b3 IRQ, b4 AFC
;    &FC11 w: adapter RAM slot   &FC12 r/w: data   &FC13 w: STATCLR
;
;  MEMORY
;    private workspace: one page (see init_workspace for the layout); on a
;                       Master it is in hidden RAM
;    terminal:  &4A00 page buffer, &4F00-&6D00 link buffers, kept pages from
;               OSHWM, &7000-&79FF Telesoftware, &7A00-&7B5F workspace
;    the page grabber stores pages in I/O processor memory only
;
;  CONVENTIONS
;    &xx hexadecimal; Lxxxx an address with no better name.
;
; =============================================================================
; SYMBOLS (RAM, zero page and I/O addresses named in this listing)
; =============================================================================
