    8124  9D F0 0D  STA rom_wksp_table,X
    8127  60        RTS
;------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; INITIALISE THE PRIVATE WORKSPACE PAGE (pointer in &84/&85):
;   +&00-&9F  20 page grabber records of 8 bytes: magazine, page, sub-code hi, lo,
;             buffer address lo, hi (+2 spare) - all &FF: not in use
;   +&A0-&B3  20 record flags: b0 HOLD, b1 RECEIVED, b2 BEING UPDATED, b3/b5 row 27 seen
;   +&B4      rows to capture per page          +&B5/&B6 record being grabbed / its magazine
;   +&B7      header status (0 off, 1 clock, &FF no clock)   +&B8 header magazine (&FF all)
;   +&B9/&BA  write pointer for the next row    +&BD   control latch shadow
;   +&BE      adapter RAM slot being read      +&BF-&D2 saved zero page &70-&83
;   +&D4-&E0  TSDP (initial page, network id, offset, MJD, UTC)
;   +&E7      subtitles (bit 7 set = off)       +&EE/&EF subtitle magazine / page
;   +&E8      rows captured so far              +&E9   interrupt mode (0 off, &FF on, &FE tune)
;   +&EA-&ED  error / byte counters for *TUNE   +&F0   magazines seen with page &FF headers
;   +&F1      row length: &2A (42, ATS format) or &28 (40, TFS compatible)
;   +&F2      last double-height row written
; On a Master (OS 3+) bit 7 is put back into the page number: the workspace is in the
; hidden RAM at &C000-&DFFF.
;------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.init_workspace
