; SERVICE 5: INTERRUPT - THE PAGE GRABBER
; Only one page is grabbed at a time: the record whose header arrived most recently
; (+&B5) in its magazine (+&B6). Zero page &70-&83 is used as scratch, so the caller's
; values are saved in the workspace and put back at the end.
; For each full adapter slot:
;   - decode magazine/row (L90F0)
;   - in tuning mode (&FE) just count bytes and Hamming errors for the meter
;   - row 0: decode the header (L9126) and
;       * show it as a rolling header at &7C08 (32 characters, or 24 when the clock
;         is replaced by HOLD), filtered by the header magazine and control bits
;       * on the subtitle page: subtitle mode, clearing the screen on "erase"
;       * finish the page being grabbed: flag RECEIVED, clear BEING UPDATED
;       * look for a record (not on HOLD) that wants this page and start grabbing it:
;         clear its buffer (rows of 42 zero bytes, or 40 spaces in TFS mode)
;   - other rows of the page being grabbed: append as 42-byte records (magazine, row,
;     40 bytes), or in TFS mode write 40 display bytes to row*40 with double height
;   - subtitle rows go straight onto the MODE 7 screen
;   - magazine 8 row 30: the service data packet (L8FAC)
; Finally clear STATCLR, save zero page back and re-enable capture.
